# Velani

> Velani is a software company operated by VELANI LLC. It makes NEVORA, an app for scheduling, time clock and payroll calculation for teams that work in shifts, and it designs and builds websites, booking apps, online stores and business tools for other businesses. The site is in English and Spanish.

Velani does not sell physical products on this site, and nothing here can be bought in a cart. To start, a business asks for a free NEVORA trial on the Plans page (online signup isn't open yet, so Velani sets up the workplace with them), or describes a project on the contact page.

## NEVORA

- [NEVORA Workforce](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/nevora): build and publish the week's schedule, shift swaps and time off answered in the app, a time clock on a shared tablet with a four-digit PIN, timecards ready for review, and payroll calculated from approved hours with pay statements. Runs on the web, in English and Spanish. The phone app is coming to the App Store and Google Play.
- [Plans](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/plans): free for 30 days with no card. After the trial, each business pays $19 a month for 1 to 15 employees or $29 a month for 16 to 30, for the whole app; owners are not counted. More than 30 employees: assisted setup by request (support@thevelani.com, reply within two business days); teams that qualify get the same 30-day trial.
- NEVORA calculates pay statements. It does not pay employees or file payroll taxes.
- Each workplace has its own NEVORA address. Owners, managers and employees sign in there with their Employee ID and password; the four-digit PIN is only for the shared tablet time clock.
- Employees get their NEVORA account from their workplace, not from this website. [NEVORA support](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/nevora-support)

## Coming later

- [Rondo in NEVORA](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/nevora#rondo): an AI assistant being built into NEVORA. In development; no release date.
- [NEVORA Relay](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/nevora#relay): orders, a kitchen display and inventory for restaurants and counters. In design; no dates. People can join the waitlist.
- Rondo on this site is a separate thing: the chat adviser on thevelani.com that answers questions about Velani and NEVORA. It can be wrong and cannot make bookings, changes or payments.

## Custom development

- [Websites, booking and rewards apps, online stores and business tools](https://www.thevelani.com/pages/custom-development), priced per project. A first conversation, then a written proposal with scope, cost and milestones; paid work starts only after the client agrees.
- Client work shown on the site: Tool Box LLC (equipment rental website and online store with delivery priced by distance) and Yavi Barber (booking and rewards app).

